    "carBox: eyeballed on a ruler over the pack photo; segModel birefnet-general (the lite model followed the blister on the other cars)",
    "wheels: traced on a 9x ruler (tyres x 134-184 and 301-351, bottoms ~560.5 on the card edge, r~25); auto-detection found only the rims (r 17-18), which put the ground ~2 px high. Mask itself checked on a zoomed ruler: wing, rear diffuser, slanted front splitter included, bottom stops at the sill (y~555), roof edge on the paint - no mask.add/remove needed",
    "size (step 2b): clean fitted length 0.999 / width 1.006 / height 1.016 vs sheet; silhouette-front/rear show the body width on the drawing (only the wing endplates differ - the front drawing is a perspective view that shrinks the far-away wing); views.html front/rear match, so no model.fit",
    "model.rebake.glass: every view traced on the mesh, none from 'sheet' - the drawing's window masks sit 3-8 px off Tripo's panels in all five views (side/left windows too high, top rear window ~60 px aft, front/rear spilled under the wing). Side + left: door window and rear quarter window traced separately on the clay's inner frame lines, leaving the slanted black B-pillar out. Top (Tripo never saw it): windscreen to the inner cowl line and rear window on the panel, upper half, glass_mirror. Front: windscreen on Tripo's dark paint / clay frame, left half, glass_mirror. Rear: both panes traced separately around the wing's centre stay (mirroring put the pane 2.5 px into the stay - the mesh is a touch off-centre)",
    "glass not tinted: the toy's windows are see-through bronze, not privacy glass",
    "model.rebake.skip top (x 168-252 over the rear window rows): the top drawing's rear window sits ~60-80 px aft of the mesh's, so it painted a glossy bronze 'glass' band onto the trunk lid behind the real window; the rear and side views paint that band now",
    "known flaw, mesh-side: Tripo's UVs overlap the windscreen with the dashboard below it; where a dashboard face wins a texel, that texel is opaque gold (a zig-zag 'M' patch upper-right of the windscreen, also present in Tripo's own paint). Not fixable from hints",
    "known flaw: the sheet's gold paint carries a swirly engraved pattern that the repaint copies; the real toy is smooth polished gold"
  ],
